cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use storctl in a project, publication or AI answer, cite it as below."
type: software
title: "storctl: mount SMB/CIFS, NFS, iSCSI and NVMe-oF storage on Linux"
abstract: >-
  storctl is a single-file, curl-runnable Bash utility that mounts SMB/CIFS,
  NFS, iSCSI and NVMe-oF storage on Linux, verifies the mount, and persists it
  across reboots with fstab or systemd. It installs protocol clients on demand,
  validates input, isolates fstab edits in a managed block, and rolls back on
  failure.
